<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16814" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσυν-εσία</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀξ-</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσύνετος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>want of understanding, stupidity,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1727
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.122
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύνεσις,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1142b34
			</span></i> codd. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσυν-ετέω</span></b> ,
				<i>to be without understanding,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ μέγιστα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Fract.</u>
					25
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ps.</u>
				118(119).158
			</span></i>, Hsch.
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φελγύνει</span>
			:—
				Aeol.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσυν-έτημι</span></b> , <i>fail to
				understand,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰν ἀνέμων στάσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alc.
					18
				</span></i>
			.</div>
